{
  "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
  "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument next in Case 05-1631, Scott versus Harris. Mr. Savrin."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Can I ask this question about the shopping center. Wouldn't your case be exactly the same if the shopping center incident had not occurred?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Is the rule that you propose that the policeman must balance the risk of harm to others versus the risk of harm to the fleeing person?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0000-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "When a suspect disobeys a lawful command to stop, races off in a reckless attempt to elude the police, and demonstrates a disregard for his own life and the lives of others in his path, the police may use force, including deadly force, to bring the suspect's vehicle flight to a halt and protect the public safety."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States (amicus curiae)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0000-0007",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The key determination is whether the officer on the scene reasonably determines that the vehicle poses a substantial risk to other motorists or the police in his way."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And a reasonable juror could not conclude to the contrary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. JONES",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0001-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Officer Scott himself admitted in his testimony that he knew at the time that he was using deadly force, and he realized at the time that he was likely to cause injury or -- death or serious injury to Mr. Harris."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Craig T. Jones",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0001-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF CRAIG T. JONES, ON BEHALF OF RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What is the standard?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Study cited by amicus briefs",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Dr. Albert testified that 70 percent of the time, when police back off pursuit, the perpetrator stops running and they resume safe driving."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice KENNEDY",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Can you tell me as of the time he exited the parking lot, by that point, had he committed any felonies?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. JONES)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0002-0001",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "No. All he had done was taken evasive action to avoid an officer who --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice GINSBURG",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0002-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The key point is that he is endangering the lives and safety of others."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. SAVRIN)",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0002-0006",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Let me refocus for a moment that in order for the officer to be denied qualified immunity in this context a jury would have to be able to find two things. One, that no -- that there was no probable cause, and second, that that was clearly established."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "b521cee14ffc1871702c4a4a007731f1af8c016a35c928000e4b7d10e0f5b19f",
      "evidence_id": "ev-b521cee14ffc-0002-0007",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-1631",
      "confidence": 0.0,
